  "change_notes": {
    "source": "DOCS/CHANGELOG.md",
    "present": true,
    "heading": "v1.45.27008 — 2026-09-17",
    "highlights": [
      "A new companion badge — a small animated porthole that occasionally signs itself with a cross or waves — is present on every screen; tap it for a dockable, resizeable chat panel that remembers where you left it.",
      "The companion streams replies on device; this build runs a deterministic preview engine while the TurboQuant engine stanza completes.",
      "Settings: the Missal tab now offers the full Mass form (Low, Cantata, Solemn) and role lens; the Journal tab gains the priest/laity exposure mode; Sync exports and restores a snapshot of your journal, homilies and preferences; Account and Library show live, truthful state instead of placeholder text.",
      "Release engineering: the debug-Android build stage is retired and the web PWA collection follows the new self-applying service-worker registration."
    ],
    "markdown": "The Companion arrives, and every Settings tab becomes real.\n\n- A new companion badge — a small animated porthole that occasionally signs itself with a cross or waves — is present on every screen; tap it for a dockable, resizeable chat panel that remembers where you left it.\n- The companion streams replies on device; this build runs a deterministic preview engine while the TurboQuant engine stanza completes.\n- Settings: the Missal tab now offers the full Mass form (Low, Cantata, Solemn) and role lens; the Journal tab gains the priest/laity exposure mode; Sync exports and restores a snapshot of your journal, homilies and preferences; Account and Library show live, truthful state instead of placeholder text.\n- Release engineering: the debug-Android build stage is retired and the web PWA collection follows the new self-applying service-worker registration."
  },
